This repository holds the source of two libraries and the scripts to build
them. Each library keeps its own licence.

FFmpeg 9.0.2, in ffmpeg/, with the changes in patches/ (which are under the
same licence as the files they change), is licensed under the GNU Lesser
General Public License version 2.1 or later. See:

    ffmpeg/COPYING.LGPLv2.1   the licence text
    ffmpeg/LICENSE.md         FFmpeg's statement of how its parts are licensed

The configuration the scripts build disables FFmpeg's GPL, nonfree and
version 3 components.

dav1d 1.5.4, which build-ffmpeg.sh fetches and links into the FFmpeg
framework, is licensed under the BSD 2-Clause licence:

    licenses/dav1d-COPYING

GNU FriBidi 1.0.16, which build-fribidi.sh fetches and builds unmodified, is
licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 or later:

    licenses/fribidi-COPYING

The build scripts, build-ffmpeg.sh and build-fribidi.sh, and README.md are
licensed under the MIT License below. That licence covers only those files:
FFmpeg, the patches to it, dav1d and FriBidi keep the licences above, and
anyone who uses, changes or distributes them must follow those licences.

